# Datetime bodies are checked with precise spans.
mode: syntax
---- query
datetime(2023-02-29) datetime(2024-13-01) datetime(now())
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..58
  PIPELINE@0..57
    LITERAL@0..20
      DATETIME@0..20 "datetime(2023-02-29)"
    WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
    ERROR@21..57
      DATETIME@21..41 "datetime(2024-13-01)"
      WHITESPACE@41..42 " "
      DATETIME@42..56 "datetime(now()"
      R_PAREN@56..57 ")"
  WHITESPACE@57..58 "\n"

error[DS0003]: invalid datetime `2023-02-29`
  --> query:1:18
  |
1 | datetime(2023-02-29) datetime(2024-13-01) datetime(now())
  |                  ^^ February 2023 has 28 days
  |
  = help: write an ISO 8601 date: `datetime(2024-01-31)` or `datetime(2024-01-31T12:00:00Z)`

error[DS0101]: expected `|` or `;`, found `datetime(2024-13-01)`
  --> query:1:22
  |
1 | datetime(2023-02-29) datetime(2024-13-01) datetime(now())
  |                      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

error[DS0003]: invalid datetime `2024-13-01`
  --> query:1:36
  |
1 | datetime(2023-02-29) datetime(2024-13-01) datetime(now())
  |                                    ^^ months are 01 to 12
  |
  = help: write an ISO 8601 date: `datetime(2024-01-31)` or `datetime(2024-01-31T12:00:00Z)`

error[DS0003]: invalid datetime `now(`
  --> query:1:52
  |
1 | datetime(2023-02-29) datetime(2024-13-01) datetime(now())
  |                                                    ^^^^ not a date
  |
  = help: write an ISO 8601 date: `datetime(2024-01-31)` or `datetime(2024-01-31T12:00:00Z)`
  = help: to convert a value to a datetime, use `todatetime(...)`
